        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Huell Howser\n- Works: California's Gold, Winnie the Pooh (2011)\n- Organizations: KCET, California PBS stations, Disney\n- Topics: television hosting, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- Huell Howser was born on October 18, 1945, and died on January 7, 2013.\n- Huell Howser was an American television personality, actor, producer, writer, singer, and voice artist.\n- Huell Howser was best known for hosting, producing, and writing California's Gold.\n- KCET in Los Angeles produced California's Gold for California PBS stations.\n- In 2011, Huell Howser voiced the Backson in Winnie the Pooh.\n- Winnie the Pooh, released in 2011, is the 51st Disney animated feature film.",
